WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.630
(ethereal music)

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:03.280
- [Angeli Gabriel] Named
after the ancient Roman

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:04.800
goddess of beauty,

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.230
Venus is known for its
exceptional brightness

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.143
in the night sky.

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:13.760
But behind this facade is a
world of storms and infernos

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.263
unlike anywhere else in the solar system.

00:00:18.723 --> 00:00:21.610
Venus, the second planet from the sun,

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:24.510
is very similar to Earth from a distance.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.590
But up close, it's a very different world.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.398
Venus is about the same size as Earth,

00:00:29.398 --> 00:00:31.540
just slightly smaller.

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:34.120
It's structure is also nearly identical,

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.748
with an iron core, a hot mantle,

00:00:35.748 --> 00:00:37.970
and a rocky crust.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.590
The crust of Venus, however,

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.890
is dotted with thousands of volcanoes,

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.730
including Maxwell Montes,

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.723
a volcano almost as tall as Mount Everest.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:52.580
Venus also has a thick layered atmosphere.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.150
It's full of clouds that rain
(thunder cracking)

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.800
sulfuric acid, and whip around the planet

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.440
at speeds up to 224 miles per hour.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.473
Faster than some category five hurricanes.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:05.920
The atmosphere is so thick

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.610
that it creates a surface pressure

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:08.790
similar to what it would be

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:12.030
about half a mile deep
in the Earth's oceans.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.610
This pressure is heavy enough

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.190
that a human standing on Venus' surface,

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:18.070
would be crushed.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:20.810
The atmosphere is made
of greenhouse gases,

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:23.050
primarily carbon dioxide.

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:26.200
Which create an extreme
case of global warming.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.750
They trap the sun's heat,

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.810
causing surface temperatures to rise

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:32.880
over 880 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:36.193
Making Venus the hottest
planet in the solar system.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:39.670
Venus is so inhospitable,

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:41.420
neither humans nor space craft

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:44.140
are able to survive the planet's surface.

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.790
But some scientists speculate

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:48.960
that Venus wasn't always so unwelcoming.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.230
From roughly 2.9 billion
to 715 million years go,

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:55.030
global temperatures on Venus

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:57.200
may have been just a few degrees cooler

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.290
than Earth's are today.

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:01.410
And scientists theorize that the surface

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.590
may have contained shallow oceans

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:06.213
that could have held enough
water to support life.

00:02:07.822 --> 00:02:09.320
(bright instrumental music)

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:14.180
Today, life may still
exist in Venus' atmosphere.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:16.800
About 30 miles up in Venus' clouds,

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.100
where the temperature and surface pressure

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.840
are similar to those on
the surface of Earth,

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.210
scientists have observed
strange dark streaks

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.440
that appear to be absorbing
ultraviolet radiation.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:30.048
A phenomenon that could be evidence

00:02:30.048 --> 00:02:30.948
of microbial life.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.100
Life may struggle to survive

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.840
in the atmosphere of Venus,

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.240
but it is this unforgiving environment

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.603
that's made Venus an icon of beauty.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.180
It reflects 70% of all the sunlight

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.630
that reaches the planet,

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:48.220
which is why Venus shines more brightly

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:51.483
than any other planet or
star in the night sky.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:56.770
While more than 40 unmanned space craft

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:59.170
have visited this infernal world,

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:02.950
Venus, so illuminated in
the darkness of space,

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.683
still has much to reveal.

